# Consumer workspaces for the Stoa substrate-update check skill.
# One absolute path per line. Comments (#) and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Used by substrate/skills/check-substrate-updates/check.sh to know which
# workspaces to scan for drift between deployed substrate files and the
# current the-stoa source.
#
# SETUP: copy this file to `consumer-workspaces.txt` (same directory) and
# replace the examples below with YOUR workspaces' absolute paths. The real
# `consumer-workspaces.txt` is gitignored — it is per-operator config and is
# never committed or shipped (your machine layout stays yours). check.sh also
# accepts `--workspace <path>` for a one-off check or `--registry <path>` to
# point at a registry elsewhere, so a registry file is optional.
#
# Example (replace with your own):
# /home/you/projects/my-consumer-workspace
# /home/you/.claude
